{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/939751-merit-contract-or-kith-blessing","id":939751,"title":"Merit, Contract or Kith blessing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-29T13:32:52-07:00","id":939751,"title":"Merit, Contract or Kith blessing","content":"How do you tell or figure out which one of the above is best for an ideal you have for a changeling ability. I've been reading the old fairy tales and love the ideal of home brewing but don't know which set of abilities is best to use as a frame work<br /> examples: Transforming one thing into another (straw into gold) permanently; Temporally changing one thing into another (pumpkin into carriage), Granting a supernatural gift to a helpful mortal or Fae touched (being able to turn into an animal or always being lucky at games of chance)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T08:25:39-07:00","id":942727,"title":"","content":"I think of Merits generally as something that has permanence that does not cost the user anything to &quot;activate.&quot; It is something built into the character or into their relationships or backstory that is not necessarily an ability. Conversely, abilities that can only be used a limited number of times per story could count as Merits (like Dream in Mage). Regardless, if it costs Glamour to activate, I would not make it a Merit.<br /> <br /> Kith blessings are blessings that reflect a fae's job or role in their durance. They are a result of what the changeling was forced to do or how they were expected to act. Contracts are agreements that the changeling has with the Hedge itself that change them and grant them powerful abilities.<br /> <br /> I distinguish between contracts and kiths based on this: is the ability something that would be unique to this changeling based on their durance, or is it the sort of thing that comes up regularly in folklore, the kind of ability that multiple changelings may have even if its manifestation is different.<br /> <br /> Under this system I would classify the items on your list as contracts (especially because there are already contracts like Skinmask and Chrysalis that deal with transforming the fae himself) and come up with an appropriate cost and catch extrapolating from the existing similar contracts. In your position I would write up the ability as you perceive it, then consider the following: (1) kith blessings tend to be flat effects that don't necessarily require dice rolls, (2) kith blessings don't have catches like contracts, so no way to get out of the cost, (3) kith blessings tend to only cost 1 point of glamour so power them appropriately and keep in mind blessings will get more use than contracts. Having said that, there's no reason you can't write up a kith description and make the kith blessing either the same as this ability or just have their kith blessing be access to the contract itself...<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it's up to you. What do you like, what do you want to see in your story? I've done a really pisspoor job of statting up your first ability as a merit, a contract, and a kith:<br /> <br /> Midas Touch (Merit) (2-3 dots): Once per story per dot of Transfigure, the changeling may convert an inanimate object of size 3 or smaller into gold, giving it all the appropriate Structure and Durability that this entails. At 3 dots the object may be up to size 5.<br /> <br /> Midas Touch (3 dot contract): Cost: 1 glamor. Dice pool: Composure + Crafts + Wyrd. The changeling can convert an inanimate object to gold, up to size determined by the number of successes. Catch: The changeling has acquired the transfigured item by deceiving a friend.<br /> <br /> Glimmerwright (Kith): Served a durance that entailed transfiguration of base objects into precious materials, whether it was painstakingly buffing simple metals into silver and gold or squeezing coals and rock into diamonds and gemstones. Blessing: The changeling gains the 9-again quality to all craft rolls involving precious metals or precious gems. She gains the Informed condition on matters dealing with raw materials. The changeling may spend one glamour to convert a common material of size 2 or smaller into a precious metal or gem. For example, he could convert a copper pipe into a gold one, or a jasper stone into a sapphire.<br /> <br /> Which of these appeals to you the most?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:01:04-07:00","id":943252,"title":"","content":"thank you alot that some very good info you gave me. I'll really have to consider it all though. I really love that you took the time to touch on all three types. My favorite of the three would have to be the contract with maybe a five point version that allows you to change a material into any other material with spending a for like maybe a scene but maybe with a exceptional success making it a permanent change.<br /> <br /> Reading the material on the Goblin markets really makes me want to create a multi tiered system for using the immaterial things that you buy or trade for in such a place. I just have this ideal of occult focused changeling capturing ghosts to power cars and building using sun beams to forge swords and clock work hand prosthetics. Sometimes I really want to play a devilish character but what do I use all the souls, memories and love i collected for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:17:58-07:00","id":943575,"title":"","content":"Just an example. Don't know if it should be a 4 dot or a 5 dot contract but I think with the additional glamour cost it &quot;feels&quot; like a 4.<br /> <br /> One Man's Trash (Contract, 4 dots): Cost: 1 glamour. Dice pool: Composure + Crafts + Wyrd. The character may transmute the material of an inanimate object of size 3 or smaller from any one material to any other. The character must be touching the object she wishes to transmute. She could, for example, turn an iron gate into one made of tin, turn a steel knife into paper, or a lead pipe into gold. The change only lasts for one scene after which the object will revert back to its original material unless doing so would be physically impossible. With an exceptional success, the character may spend an additional point of glamour to make the change Lasting. Catch: The changeling has acquired the item by deceiving a friend, or intends to deceive a friend with the tranmuted object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:07:35-07:00","id":943855,"title":"","content":"For blessing a mortal, its possible to interrupt Goblin Vows in such a way that you can Seal someone elses pledge to aspects of the Wyrd instead of to yourself, not just seal your own pledges to aspects of the wyrd, or seal peoples pledges to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> So a mortal could promise to feed your rabbits for a week, which you use your goblin vow &quot;rabbits&quot; to seal to that aspect of the Wyrd, granting him the fleet of foot merit as a reward for a period of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:53:22-07:00","id":943904,"title":"","content":"Huh that's an awesome ideal I never would of thought that you could use goblin vows that way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}